WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.947
People naturally rely on intuition, experience, and mental shortcuts when making decisions.

2
00:00:05.947 --> 00:00:12.412
These approaches can be useful, but they can also introduce blind spots, overconfidence, and bias.

3
00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:20.265
Structured analytic techniques provide methods for slowing down thinking, challenging assumptions, and making reasoning more transparent.

4
00:00:20.265 --> 00:00:23.458
They help analysts show how they moved from evidence to judgment.

5
00:00:23.458 --> 00:00:26.192
These techniques do not replace expertise.

6
00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:35.790
Instead, they help analysts use expertise more effectively when dealing with uncertainty, incomplete information, and competing explanations.

7
00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:37.986
The value of structure is discipline.

8
00:00:37.986 --> 00:00:47.464
It gives teams repeatable ways to ask better questions, surface uncertainty, compare possibilities, and communicate judgments with appropriate confidence.
